      "title": "Associations in Data",
      "purpose": "Students construct and interpret scatter plots for bivariate data to investigate patterns of association between two quantities. They describe patterns such as clustering and outliers. Students informally fit a line to model the association in data and assess how well the line fits the data. For scatter plots that suggest a linear association, they interpret the slope and *y*-intercept in context and use the linear model to make predictions. Students use two-way tables and segmented bar graphs to make claims about associations in categorical data.",
